---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Admin portal"
  path="/docs/user-guide/admin-portal"
  description="Daily work in the KoAkademy administration panel and admin workspace — records, enrollment, finance, and system management."
>
  <p>
    Administrative staff work in two connected areas: the
    <strong>administration panel</strong> at <code>/admin</code> (records, resources,
    and settings) and the <strong>admin workspace</strong> (guided operational screens
    such as enrollment processing and finance). What you see depends on your role
    and permissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Sign-in and security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Sign in with your staff account. Administrators can require
      <strong>two-factor authentication</strong> (authenticator app or e-mail code)
      and <strong>passkeys</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the <strong>school-year and semester selector</strong> in the panel header
      before entering data, so records land in the correct academic period.
    </li>
    <li>
      Press <span class="doc-kbd">Ctrl</span>+<span class="doc-kbd">L</span>
      (Windows/Linux) or <span class="doc-kbd">⌘</span>+<span class="doc-kbd"
        >L</span
      >
      (macOS) for global search across students, classes, and other records.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Dashboard</h2>
  <p>
    The panel dashboard summarizes operations with widgets: enrollment,
    retention, and attrition statistics, demographics, scholarship distribution,
    clearance status, geographic distribution, recent enrollments and students,
    resource availability, and upcoming events. Widgets respect the selected
    academic period and your permissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Records and resources</h2>
  <p>The sidebar groups the core resources:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Resource</th>
        <th>Typical work</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Students</td>
        <td
          >Student profiles, documents, signature capture, enrollment
          checklists, clearances</td
        >
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Student Enrollments</td>
        <td>Enrollment records, statuses, and history</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Faculties and Accounts</td>
        <td>Teaching staff and user accounts</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Courses and Departments</td>
        <td>Programs, curriculum structure, and departments</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Classes and Rooms</td>
        <td>Sections, schedules, capacity, and room assignment</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Events</td>
        <td>School calendar events shown on dashboards</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Schools</td>
        <td>Institutions in a multi-school deployment</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Users and Roles</td>
        <td>Accounts, role assignment, and permission review</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Senior High School</td>
        <td>SHS strands and SHS student records (cluster)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Additional panel pages cover <strong>Timetable</strong> management,
    <strong>Student Clearances</strong>, <strong>Backups</strong>, and
    <strong>General Settings</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Enrollment processing</h2>
  <p>The admin workspace provides the operational enrollment flow:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Search and review applicants.</strong> Look up a student and open their
      application.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Verify academically.</strong> The registrar or department head verifies
      subjects, documents, and assessment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Verify payment.</strong> The cashier confirms or records payment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Complete or reopen.</strong> Finish the enrollment, or use the authorized
      undo/reopen action with a reason.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Enrollment reports, analytics, and assessment PDFs are available from the
    same area. Configuration of availability, eligibility, tuition, and
    approvals is handled by <strong>Enrollment Blueprints</strong> — see the Blueprint
    guides in the documentation navigation.
  </p>

  <h2>Finance</h2>
  <p>
    The finance area provides dashboards, payment recording, invoices and
    receipts, and reports. Statements of account can be issued to students and
    include a signed public verification link. Bulk assessment PDFs are
    generated in the background; downloads appear when ready.
  </p>

  <h2>System management</h2>
  <p>
    The System Management area centralizes institution configuration: school
    profile and branding, academic periods, grading rules, student identifier
    formats, mail delivery, notification templates, analytics, SEO, social
    sign-in providers, API keys, and the <strong>Feature Toggles</strong> page that
    switches portal features on or off.
  </p>
  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">Audit trail</p>
    <p>
      Administrative changes are recorded under <strong>Audit Logs</strong>.
      When something looks wrong, check there first before changing a record
      back.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
